The project details and documentation
IMU-Based Roll Angle Estimation and PWM Control (STM32) – Ongoing
•	Integrated MPU6050 IMU sensor on STM32, including analysis and resolution of I²C communication issues (ACK, pin mapping) via register-level debugging
•	Developed I²C read/write drivers using STM32 HAL for power management, sampling rate, and sensor configuration
•	Implemented roll angle estimation from raw accelerometer data and derived a PWM control signal based on system orientation
•	Configured STM32 timers for PWM generation and dynamically adjusted duty cycle using real-time sensor data
•	Applied signal conditioning (scaling, clamping, dead-zone logic) to stabilize control behavior and reduce noise
•	Validated and debugged system behavior using LED as an actuator

